Package: psychdsish
Title: Keep Data, R Code, and Outputs Organized and Reproducible
Version: 0.2.2
Authors@R:
    person("Ian", "Hussey", email = "ian.hussey@unibe.ch",
           role = c("aut", "cre", "cph"),
           comment = c(ORCID = "0000-0001-8906-7559"))
Description: Creates a standardised project skeleton for research projects
    in R that is loosely inspired by the 'psych-DS' data standard
    (<https://psych-ds.github.io/>) for psychological data, and checks
    whether an existing project follows the same conventions. The layout is
    not fully 'psych-DS' compliant -- most notably it drops the JSON
    metadata requirement -- hence 'psych-DS-ish'. Single- and multi-study
    projects are supported. Alongside the directory structure it generates
    'Quarto' templates for processing and analysis code (including a
    codebook for the processed data), a README, a licence, a citation file,
    a '.gitignore' with sensible defaults, and a 'Quarto' project file that
    renders the code in order. A validator function reports whether a
    project follows the conventions, including whether raw data have
    changed since they were first committed to 'Git' and whether rendered
    reports are up to date, and, where it does not, how to fix it. 'RStudio'
    users can create projects from the New Project wizard and validate them
    from the Addins menu. See Hussey (2026) <doi:10.5281/zenodo.21441984>
    for the archived software record.
URL: https://github.com/ianhussey/psychdsish
BugReports: https://github.com/ianhussey/psychdsish/issues
